column4:
) and the `/outstanding` skill's ownership section (doesn't mention pre-existing files). Genuinely new.
- `no-chat-in-code` — the closest is not a rule of yours but Claude Code's built-in prompt, which already bans comments explaining "where it came from" or "why your change is correct". So this one is roughly half-covered out of the box; its marginal value is the concrete banned-phrase list ("no longer", "was previously", …) and the present-tense prescription. If you land only one of the two, drop this one.

Nothing has been moved or written; both decisions are still open — tell me which way.
